      "id": "1577299816392306689",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "17664709",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 3,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1577289365939683328",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "@gwern Don’t overrotate on my initial use of the word “style”.\n\nBy using the artists name in the prompt, you’re invariably going to use IP that belongs to the artist. Maybe not every generation, but most of them. \n\nYou can’t possibly want artists to get disenfranchised by generative AI?",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1577299816392306689"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1576815967371292672",
